174:Saturne
175:{character:player} I'm very sorry, sir, but the café's rules don't allow us to stay too long with customers.
176:{character:Saturne} Ah well, that is a pity. I do hope we have the chance to meet again. And should we do, you be sure to accept my invitation then, hmm?
177:{character:player} Of course.
178:{character:player} That customer today, Saturne. Does he often order deliveries?
179:{character:Reina Nanami} Saturne? No, not at all. That peculiar order certainly jumped out at me, and if I recall correctly today is the first time he's placed an order with us.
180:{character:player} As long as I'm not imposing, I'd be delighted to.
181:{character:Saturne} Marvelous! Thank you! I trust we shall have a simply splendid afternoon.
182:{character:Saturne} If I'd known I was going to invite you, I would have prepared some good tea or wine. However, if it wasn't for these two bottles of sparkling orange, I would never have made your acquaintance in the first place! How marvelous life can be!
183:{character:player} I think the sparkling orange is excellent. It is a specialty of Éternité, after all.
184:{character:player} Could I ask you something? Seeing as the main attraction of Éternité is the various kinds of coffee, not that many people specifically order the sparkling orange. You must really like it, right?
185:{character:Saturne} My hometown is very far away and exceedingly cold. We have neither oranges nor this kind of sparkling beverage. Basically, where I live these sorts of things are almost impossible to find so... Perhaps the rarity makes them valuable to me.
186:{character:player} So are you here in One Han City for business, sir?
187:{character:Saturne} Ha, you could say that. As a businessman, I'm often in town closing deals. Sometimes negotiations drag on, however, which is why I bought this place as a home away from home.
188:{character:Saturne} I was seeking peace and quiet when I bought it, but peace and quiet can be so tedious sometimes. That's why I like to entertain people these days.
189:{character:player} Don't worry, it's just a simple delivery. There's no bad job, just bad workers!
190:{character:???} Hello! Is there a table free?
191:{character:player} Certainly. Please, follow me.
192:{character:???} Um, excuse me... It's my first time coming to this sort of café, so I'm just really curious, but I don't mean anything by it. By the way, I'm Eve Krist. You can call me Eve.
193:{character:player} Hi, Eve. I'm {var:player_nickname}, I'll serve you today.
194:{character:Eve Krist} {var:player_nickname}. That's a lovely name. When you have a minute, would you mind accompanying me for a while?
196:{character:Hinata Takanashi} {var:player_nickname}, if you're busy then I'd be happy to look after this guest. Relax, I'll make sure she gets the absolute best service!
197:{character:player} Thanks, I appreciate it.
198:{character:Eve Krist} This person... Looks so familiar, eh... The name's on the tip of my tongue... Don't tell me! I have an excellent memory, I can... Oh, what was it... Stop shaking... Urgh... So dizzy...
199:{character:Hinata Takanashi} Ahahaha... She seems to be drunk on coffee!
200:{character:player} Drunk on coffee?
201:{character:Hinata Takanashi} Boss gave us training on this before. Some people just naturally can't handle caffeine, and have side effects if they drink coffee... To be honest though, I never thought someone would have this severe a reaction—and just after a single cup, too!
202:{character:player} Eve! Eve?! Are you alright?
203:{character:Eve Krist} No, not really... I'm so very dizzy, like I drank a whole barrel of wine.
204:{character:player} ...
205:{character:Eve Krist} I'm so sorry for all the trouble I caused today.
206:{character:player} It's fine, just as long as you're okay. We forgot to warn you that some people can have quite strong adverse reactions to caffeine, so it's kind of our fault.
207:{character:Eve Krist} There's no coffee in Northland, so no cafés, only hotels and inns. I was always under the impression that drinking coffee was the same as drinking wine, which I'm rather good at. I never thought that my tolerance for caffeine would not even handle one full cup!
208:{character:player} I don't think... That's how it works...
209:{character:Eve Krist} I'm sorry, but I must go. Please accept my most sincere apologies once more, for any trouble I may have caused you today.
210:{character:Eve Krist} Nonetheless, I must say the coffee here is really nice. I hope that tomorrow you could choose a few different kinds for me to challenge! I won't be beaten by a single cup again!
211:{character:Hinata Takanashi} Miss Eve reminds me of a summer's breeze.
