356:Decline the invitation
357:Yet another busy day has flashed by. I've discovered that delivering orders is yet another new experience. Over the next few days, if there are more of this kind of nearby deliveries, maybe I could give A-37 a hand?
358:Eve Krist
359:I glance awkwardly towards the cat tree where, because A-37 has gone on a delivery, the kittens he'd been looking after are already starting a "rebellion". Someone needs to go and rein them in.
361:What surprises me is that, although Eve seems to be slender, with a body that most women would die for, she is unexpectedly heavy. Her right arm, draped over me, is not only heavy but also so cold that it doesn't feel like human skin.
362:Luckily she is still sober enough to walk on her own. If she'd been fully unconscious, Hinata and I might not have been able to get her into the staff room at all.

